# Normalise line endings on checkout.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF when
# you clone. That is invisible until something treats a lone backslash or a
# shebang as significant — a CSS string continuation stops terminating, a shell
# script gains a \r in its interpreter line, and a .sql or Dockerfile mounted
# into a Linux container carries stray carriage returns.
#
# Pinning LF here means every clone gets the bytes CI and the containers expect,
# whatever each developer's git config says.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mp3   binary
